// A binary search tree that inserts top-down, by mutating the tree it walks.
//
// Two things about Cufet decide the whole shape of this program.
//
// A node cannot hold a node BY VALUE — that would be a struct containing itself, with no end
// and no fixed size — so each link is a `series of node` holding either nothing or one child.
// An empty series is "no child here", which is the same indirection `arbtree` uses, spelled to
// make the two sides of a search tree tell them apart.
//
// The second is sharper, and it is why `permanently` is on the rank. An object is a VALUE:
// pull a node out of a series and you hold a copy, so writing to its rank changes nothing that
// anyone else can see. In a search tree that is the worst possible bug — every key stays where
// the old ordering put it, the structure still looks perfectly well formed, and every later
// search silently walks the wrong way. `permanently` turns that quiet nothing into a refusal at
// check time. Nothing else in the language expresses "set when the node is made, never after".
//
// A series field is the exception: it is a region, so it is SHARED rather than copied. That is
// what makes insertion work at all — `child` below is a copy of a node, but its links are the
// real ones, so attaching through the copy attaches to the tree.

Define empty-slot as "·" permanently.
Define indent-step as "   " permanently.
Define separator as ", " permanently.

Define object node with (the number rank permanently,
                         the series of node left,
                         the series of node right):

    // Insertion walks down and attaches at the first empty link. Duplicates are dropped, which
    // is the choice that keeps `holds` an exact answer rather than a first-of-several.
    Bind void to insert-value, given (the number value):
        If value is one's rank, Return.

        If value is less than one's rank:
            If the number of one's left is 0:
                Insert (cast leaf on (value)) into one's left.
                Return.
            Done.
            // A copy of the child, whose links are the child's own — see the header.
            Define child as item 1 of one's left.
            Cast child's insert-value on (value).
            Return.
        Done.

        If the number of one's right is 0:
            Insert (cast leaf on (value)) into one's right.
            Return.
        Done.
        Define right-child as item 1 of one's right.
        Cast right-child's insert-value on (value).
    Done.

    Bind fact to holds, given (the number value):
        If value is one's rank, Return true.

        If value is less than one's rank:
            If the number of one's left is 0, Return false.
            Define child as item 1 of one's left.
            Return cast child's holds on (value).
        Done.

        If the number of one's right is 0, Return false.
        Define right-child as item 1 of one's right.
        Return cast right-child's holds on (value).
    Done.

    // In order: left, self, right — which for a search tree is ascending order, and is the cheapest
    // way to show that every insertion landed where it belonged.
    Bind void to collect-into, given (the series of number out):
        If the number of one's left is greater than 0:
            Define child as item 1 of one's left.
            Cast child's collect-into on (out).
        Done.

        Insert one's rank into out.

        If the number of one's right is greater than 0:
            Define right-child as item 1 of one's right.
            Cast right-child's collect-into on (out).
        Done.
    Done.

    Bind number to height:
        Define left-height as 0.
        If the number of one's left is greater than 0:
            Define child as item 1 of one's left.
            The left-height becomes cast child's height.
        Done.

        Define right-height as 0.
        If the number of one's right is greater than 0:
            Define right-child as item 1 of one's right.
            The right-height becomes cast right-child's height.
        Done.

        Define deeper as left-height when left-height is greater than right-height,
                         otherwise right-height.
        Return deeper + 1.
    Done.

    // Right child above, left child below, so the drawing reads the way the tree is ordered.
    //
    // A missing child is marked only on a node that HAS one, because that is the only place the
    // mark carries information: it says which side is empty. Printing it under a leaf as well
    // would double the drawing to say "a leaf has no children", which the reader already knows.
    Bind void to draw, given (the text pad):
        Define has-children as (the number of one's left + the number of one's right) is greater than 0.
        If has-children, cast draw-link on (one's right, pad).
        State "{pad}{one's rank}".
        If has-children, cast draw-link on (one's left, pad).
    Done.
Done.

// A fresh leaf, so the three-empty-series literal is written once rather than at every insert.
Bind node to leaf, given (the number value):
    Return a new node { the rank value, the left a series of node, the right a series of node }.
Done.

// A series cannot go into a text hole — a hole takes exactly what `converted to text` takes, and
// a series is not on that list — so this is how one reaches a sentence.
Bind text to as-line, given (the series of number ns):
    Define out as "".
    Define i as 1.
    While i is less than the number of ns + 1, repeat:
        If i is greater than 1, the out becomes out joined to separator.
        The out becomes out joined to "{item i of ns}".
        The i becomes i + 1.
    Done.
    Return out.
Done.

// Draws one link, present or not. A link is a series, so "no child" is something this can be
// handed and print — which a method on `node` could not be, there being no node to call it on.
Bind void to draw-link, given (the series of node link, the text pad):
    If the number of link is 0:
        State "{pad}{indent-step}{empty-slot}".
        Return.
    Done.
    Define child as item 1 of link.
    Cast child's draw on (pad joined to indent-step).
Done.

Pull a rabbit.
    Define values as a series of number with (50, 30, 70, 20, 40, 60, 80, 30, 65).

    Define root as cast leaf on (item 1 of values).
    Define i as 2.
    While i is less than the number of values + 1, repeat:
        Cast root's insert-value on (item i of values).
        The i becomes i + 1.
    Done.

    Define walked as a series of number.
    Cast root's collect-into on (walked).

    State "inserted:  {cast as-line on (values)}".
    State "in order:  {cast as-line on (walked)}".

    Define tall as cast root's height.
    Define level-word as "level" when tall is 1, otherwise "levels".
    State "height:    {tall} {level-word}".
    State "".

    Cast root's draw on ("").
    State "".

    For each probe in a series of number with (40, 65, 45, 80), repeat:
        Define verdict as "found" when cast root's holds on (probe), otherwise "missing".
        State "{probe}: {verdict}".
    Done.
Done.
